[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4029170057","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117267#issuecomment-4029170057","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117267","id":4029170057,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7wKEGJ","user":{"login":"D-SehKim","id":123012677,"node_id":"U_kgDOB1UGRQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/123012677?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/D-SehKim","html_url":"https://github.com/D-SehKim","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/D-SehKim/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/D-SehKim/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/D-SehKim/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/D-SehKim/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/D-SehKim/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/D-SehKim/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/D-SehKim/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/D-SehKim/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/D-SehKim/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-10T07:03:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-10T07:23:10Z","body":"I think this might be intended.  in ```/godot/editor/settings/event_listener_line_edit.cpp``` theres a section which reads:\n\n```cpp\n// First event will be an event which is used to focus this control - i.e. a mouse click, or a tab press.\n// Ignore the first one so that clicking into the LineEdit does not override the current event.\n// Ignore is reset to true when the control is unfocused.\n// This class also specially handles grab_focus() calls.\nif (ignore_next_event) {\n\tignore_next_event = false;\n\treturn;\n}\n```\n\nIf possible I think it could be changed to make navigating easier because currently it is kind of annoying.  I see what you mean when navigating, all controls (even right and left arrow) are considered \"events\", and therefore captured by the searchbox, and then all subsequent \"events\" are ignored and searched for instead, but we'd have to see what the maintainers think.  \n\nEdit 1: I forgot to mention what the snippet does, I believe that when the user does an \"event\" on the \"LineEdit/TextBox\", it will:\n1. Ignore the first event\n2. Focus the textbox\n3. Capture all input as a \"search\"\nThe snippet is basically showing that when interacting with the text box in any way (whether that be through tabbing through, or clicking on it, or using arrow keys to navigate), it will capture all input after the first one (which in our case, is the one we're using to navigate to it)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4029170057/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4030498119","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117267#issuecomment-4030498119","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117267","id":4030498119,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7wPIVH","user":{"login":"Giganzo","id":158825920,"node_id":"U_kgDOCXd9wA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/158825920?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giganzo","html_url":"https://github.com/Giganzo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giganzo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giganzo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giganzo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giganzo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giganzo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Giganzo/orgs","repos_url":"https:/